# .env.offline.template — offline hospital server deployment
#
# This is a TEMPLATE, not live configuration. install_offline.sh copies it
# to /opt/rah/apps/hcopilot/compose/.env on first install and overwrites the
# MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD / DATABASE_PASSWORD placeholders below with a freshly
# generated password — you never need to edit a password here by hand.
#
# The resulting .env is persistent deployment state: it lives under
# /opt/rah/apps/hcopilot/, not inside this release folder, and routine
# updates (update_offline.sh) never touch it once created.
#
# SHARED SQL SERVER INSTANCE: if this offline server already runs a SQL Server
# container for another RAH Lab project, do NOT start a second sqlserver
# service — instead:
#   1. Remove/comment out the `sqlserver` and `db-init` service blocks you
#      don't need (or just set DATABASE_SERVER below to that instance's
#      container name / host and keep db-init pointed at it).
#   2. Set DATABASE_SERVER to the existing instance's hostname or container name.
#   3. Make sure DATABASE_NAME below is unique to HCopilot so it doesn't
#      collide with another project's database on the same instance.

# Replaced with a generated password by install_offline.sh — the value here
# is only used if you create .env by hand instead of running the installer.
MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD=__GENERATE_ME__
DATABASE_NAME=HCopilotDB
DATABASE_USER=sa
DATABASE_PASSWORD=__GENERATE_ME__
DATABASE_PORT=1433

BACKEND_PORT=8090
FRONTEND_PORT=8082
